  "body": "I had some questions about the mechanics of the new shadow banning merge from issue #9209 \r\n\r\nActually, only one question, but that issue was closed because apparently, folks just can't coherently discuss the technical aspects of some particular features on the technical merits of those features alone. So here's my question.\r\n\r\nWhen a server admin (because it's not available to room admins) affects this feature on say, a spammer or list bully that has proven that they're just not going away and continues to create new accounts to abuse a particular, or multiple rooms, does this retroactively ghost, or make invisible, or shadow (whatever terminology is being used) the abuser's previous posts as well, or does the shadow ban merely cover posts from that point forward?\r\n\r\nThanks :)\r\n",
